WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:04.650
A researcher with a clipboard stands
just inside the front door of a gym.

2
00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:07.830
Everyone who walks in
is asked one question:

3
00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:10.050
do you love going to the gym?

4
00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:11.260
The results are in.

5
00:00:11.310 --> 00:00:13.660
Ninety per cent say yes.

6
00:00:13.710 --> 00:00:16.430
So what does that tell us
about people in general?

7
00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:18.920
Is ninety per cent just a clear result?

8
00:00:18.970 --> 00:00:21.280
Or were too few people asked?

9
00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:23.950
In this mission, you'll
separate the population,

10
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:28.370
the whole group you want to know about,
from the sample you actually asked.

11
00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:32.800
You'll meet opportunity sampling, which
uses whoever is available at the time

12
00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:34.380
and place you collect.

13
00:00:34.430 --> 00:00:37.930
And you'll judge when a
sample is likely to be biased.

14
00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:42.030
Your mission: decide what that
ninety per cent really tells you.
